## 5. Milestones

### [CXC-RM-M0] M0 — Live, Interactive Desktop-Skia
- goal: Turn the raster-only Skia backend into a live windowed surface with an event loop feeding the engine. Formalize the `Canvas` contract as a single source of truth with a conformance test both Python-Skia and C++/CYD must pass.
- unlocks: Any interactive rendering at all — preview, then Composer. The pixel-verification baseline.
- deliverables: Skia live window on **macOS and Raspberry Pi** (windowed on macOS; fullscreen/kiosk via DRM-KMS or Wayland on RPi — RPi may need skia-python built for aarch64 or a GL surface) + run loop; pointer/keyboard/touch capture → engine events; contract conformance suite (reference shapes).
- reuse: `render/skia_backend.py` (add windowing to the working raster path), `render/canvas.py`, existing `render/widgets/` (5 widgets), `pixel_comparison.py`.
- acceptance: the 5 agnostic widgets render live in a Skia window; a bus value change updates within one frame ([CXC-R-C4]); a mouse click reaches the backend; both backends pass the conformance suite ([CXC-R-C2]).
- status: operational (first pass, 2026-07-06) — `render/window.py` `SkiaWindow(SkiaCanvas)`: SDL2 window presents the raster surface; SDL pointer/key/touch/wheel events → engine `PointerEvent`/`KeyEvent`/`WindowEvent`; 60fps sustained windowed on macOS (verified `tests/render/smoke_live_window.py`, 6/6 checks incl. window==reference at 100.00% identical AND `SDL_RenderReadPixels` presented-pixel readback at max_delta 0 — the readback catches N32 channel-order bugs that surface reads cannot see: N32 is RGBA on the macOS wheel, BGRA on Linux/aarch64, and the texture format is now selected from the surface colorType). Conformance suite `render/conformance.py`: 11 contract scenes + goldens (`conformance_golden/`), capability-tagged so the CYD subset SKIPs rather than FAILs unimplemented primitives; Skia self-verifies 11/11 at 100.00%. CYD hardware run of the suite pending device access (scenes are contract-only and mirror the crosscheck harness).
- rpi-confirmed: SAME build on (a private host name, not published) (RPi 5, aarch64, Debian 12, skia-python 144 == macOS version): conformance 11/11 against the macOS-generated goldens (geometry+atlas-text pixel-identical across OS/arch); engine acceptance tests green; LIVE window on the Wayland kiosk at 59.8fps with presented-pixel readback max_delta 0. Two RPi requirements: (1) system SDL2 via `PYSDL2_DLL_PATH=/usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu` — the bundled pysdl2-dll build hangs against this compositor; (2) typeface cache in the backend — Linux fontconfig `MakeFromName` cost ~1.5ms/call and dragged a frame from 2.2ms to 37ms before caching.
- change: "Windowed presentation = SDL2 streaming-texture blit of the SAME raster surface the pixel harness diffs; not a Skia GPU surface."
- context_for_change:
  - prior_state: "present() was a no-op; the assumed windowing path was GLFW + Skia GL surface."
  - reasoning: "Blitting the raster reference makes the on-screen pixels byte-identical to the golden PNGs (verified 100.00% identical), collapsing 'window fidelity' into the existing pixel gate. SDL2 also carries the RPi path (KMSDRM/Wayland/X11) with zero code change, where GLFW cannot do KMSDRM."
  - rejected_alternative: "GLFW + GPU surface — macOS-deprecated GL, and a GPU rasterizer's AA differs subtly from the raster reference, splitting the golden set."
  - counter_argument: "CPU raster + full-surface blit may not scale to large/high-DPI surfaces."
  - counter_response: "Measured: 960x620 full redraw ~1ms, blit <1ms (GL render driver on macOS; Metal driver blocked ~8ms/present and was bypassed). A GPU surface can be added behind SkiaWindow later without touching the Canvas contract."
  - invalidating_assumption: "That target surfaces stay ≤~2MP at 60fps on CPU raster. If a 4K/120Hz surface becomes a real target, revisit the GPU-surface path."
- part-of: [PROJECT:CXC-ROADMAP]

### [CXC-RM-M1] M1 — Layer 2 Engine (the meaty core)
- goal: Build the platform-independent engine: layout (flex + the **pixel-stack container** from the Composer UX work + grid), hit-testing/pointer dispatch, focus, animation (interpolation/easing), asset manager (`doc://` fetch + cache), and the **`.compose.yaml` → widget-tree parser**.
- unlocks: Config-driven, interactive rendering independent of backend. This is the single biggest value step.
- deliverables: engine modules per [CXC-R-ENGINE]; `.compose.yaml` parser; layout managers incl. pixel-stack; hit-test; animation; asset manager. Text-editing may be partial (defer IME).
- reuse: [SPEC:CXC-RENDER] §4 as the contract; the pixel-stack layout mode we designed for Composer.
- acceptance: load a `.compose.yaml` → correct layout + data binding on the M0 window ([CXC-R-C3], [CXC-R-C7]); click dispatches to the correct widget ([CXC-R-C6]); gauge animates at 60fps desktop ([CXC-R-C11]); config change re-renders ([CXC-R-C10]).
- status: operational (first pass, 2026-07-06) — `render/engine/` package: `layout.py` (FlexContainer + GridContainer + **PixelStackContainer**, two-pass measure/arrange), `runtime.py` (RenderApp event loop: hit-test topmost-first, tap/long-press/pan gesture synthesis, pointer capture, `_app/render/interaction` publishing per [CXC-R-CONTROL]), `focus.py` (tap-focus + Tab cycling + engine-drawn ring), `animation.py` (property interpolation, 5 easings), `assets.py` (bus://+doc://+file:// fetch/cache via composeio.resolve; verified against live bus_storage), `parser.py` (BOTH dialects: nested spec widgets/children AND the production modules/grid_row dialect — unported production widget types render as honest PlaceholderWidgets pending M2). Acceptance evidence: `tests/render/test_engine_m0_m1.py` (14 tests: C2/C3/C4/C6/C7/C10/C11) green on macOS AND RPi5/aarch64; live-window smoke 6/6 on macOS incl. presented-pixel readback; MQTT end-to-end against NODERED_HOST broker updated a gauge in 14ms.
- deferred-in-first-pass: text editing (no TextInput on the contract until M2), pinch/multitouch recognition, dirty-REGION redraw (full-frame redraw at 60fps measured cheap: ~1ms macOS / ~2.2ms RPi5 at 960x620), spec-14 `use:` component stamping in the engine parser.
- known-gap-fonts: macOS↔Linux text is NOT pixel-identical (fontconfig resolves different faces; geometry scenes match at 100%). The atlas covers only 6-16px (CYD sizes). Resolution needs the [CXC-R-DRAW-FONT] decision: bundle ONE licensed TTF as a bus asset, load via Typeface.MakeFromFile on all desktop backends, regenerate the CYD atlas from the same file. Escalated to David (font choice = product/licensing decision).
- depends-on: [CXC-RM-M0]
- part-of: [PROJECT:CXC-ROADMAP]

### [CXC-RM-M2] M2 — Widget Parity on the Contract (retires CTk on desktop)
- goal: Port the ~11 production CTk widgets (Button, Relay, Command, TextInput, Checkbox, PowerToggle, DocPicker, BusMonitor, Tab, Coordinate) plus Image + Callout (the M31 flagship) to the `Canvas` contract as agnostic `Widget` subclasses. Single Python source of truth.
- resolved-inputs (2026-07-06, David): (1) font = **IBM Plex Sans + IBM Plex Mono** — bundle as a bus asset, regenerate the CYD atlas from the same file, bake widget goldens against it once; record in [CXC-R-DRAW-FONT] via `change`/`context_for_change`. (2) `decode_image(bytes)` **promoted to the `Canvas` contract** — add to the Python ABC + `cyd/include/canvas.h`, keep the Skia impl, record normatively in [CXC-R-DRAW] via `change`/`context_for_change`.
- unlocks: **The gate that makes CTk removable on macOS + Raspberry Pi** — the workhorse runtimes where CTk actually runs.
- deliverables: full widget set on the contract, each with reference screenshots + regression tests. The existing CTk renderers are the visual spec for each port.
- reuse: `composeio_renderers/*` (visual logic to match), `render/widget.py` base, pixel-diff harness.
- acceptance: the current dashboard + ComposeUX composition render via the engine at parity with the CTk version, within pixel tolerance ([CXC-R-C1]). CTk can now be demoted to reference role.
- status: operational (2026-07-06) — all 12 widgets on the contract as agnostic Widget subclasses (`render/widgets/`): Button (all 5 led_behaviors), Relay (true visuals, replaces the M1 LED approximation), Command (arm-confirm gate replaces the OS dialog; ${ns} runtime resolution; host runner via EngineContext.invoke), TextInput (engine-native single-line editing: focus/cursor/keyboard/SDL text events, secret→$6$ hash, [CXC-R-C8] proven on the live SDL path), Checkbox, PowerToggle, DocPicker (threaded doc-store query; verified against the LIVE document_store), BusMonitor (bus.on_message, color-coded), Tab (segmented bar; "all" routing semantics — active_only unsubscribe optimization deliberately dropped), Coordinate (multi-namespace arm/status/coordinates), Image (fit modes + decode_image contract path), Callout (M31 flagship CalloutOverlayWidget — first realization, no CTk precedent). Parser resolves every production type + spec-14 `components:`/`use:` stamping (engine/components.py) — test_dashboard, minnow-bringup, and fleet-540-soak render with ZERO placeholders. Runtime M2 additions: thread-safe update queue (bus/runner callbacks → render thread, [CXC-R-C4] still one-frame), pointer down/up hooks, text-event routing, EngineContext.invoke/launch. Evidence: 179 tests green macOS AND 175 green RPi5 (goldens baked on macOS, byte-compared on RPi); 15 M2 golden scenes; conformance 12/12 both platforms incl. the new text_native scene at 100.00%/max_delta 0; full compositions macOS↔RPi: m31_flagship byte-identical (0/263k px), test_dashboard 6/576k px ≤5 delta (stroke-arc AA edge); live-window interaction smoke 9/9 (macOS), RPi kiosk loop 59.5fps with bus-driven gauge.
- font-outcome: David's two resolved inputs landed, with one measured correction recorded in [CXC-R-DRAW-FONT]: bundling Plex + Typeface.MakeFromFile was NOT sufficient for pixel identity (platform glyph scalers differ, ~8% text pixels diverged) — desktop text is now rasterized by the engine itself via pinned freetype-py and blitted, giving 100.00% cross-platform text identity; CYD atlas regenerated from the same Plex faces. decode_image is on both contracts (Python ABC + canvas.h; ESP32 stub returns nullptr pending M5).
- ctk-status: parity proven; CTk demotable to reference role. Actual retirement is a separate David call (per kickoff). Known visual divergences vs CTk, accepted: GaugeWidget keeps its Phase-1 ComposeUX design (gauge was not in the M2 port list); grid rows top-pack instead of CTk's equal-weight vertical spreading; confirm gates are engine-native arm-confirm instead of OS dialogs.
- deferred-from-m2: TextInput multiline/IME ([CXC-R-ENGINE-TEXT] P2/P3); Tab active_only dynamic bus unsubscribe; DocPicker scrollbar visuals; CYD firmware rebuild against the regenerated Plex font_atlas.h (header is committed; on-device verify pending device access — CYD stays POC-priority).
- depends-on: [CXC-RM-M1]
- part-of: [PROJECT:CXC-ROADMAP]

### [CXC-RM-CTK-RETIRE] CTk Retirement Review — Divergences Dispositioned (2026-07-06, David)
- decision: With M2 parity proven, CTk is cleared to **demote** (stop depending on it); actual deletion is a later mechanical step. The accepted CTk↔engine divergences were reviewed:
- blessed: (1) **arm-confirm replaces OS confirmation dialogs** (Command/PowerToggle) — OS modals don't exist on CYD/browser, break the pixel gate, and aren't bus-native/Intelligence-drivable; arm-confirm is portable and safer. (2) **Gauge keeps its ComposeUX design** as canonical (CTk's was interim). (4) **Tab keeps hidden tabs subscribed** ("all" routing) — warm state enables event-driven auto-focus to a hidden tab (e.g. a "Damage Control" tab that fires on a hit); `active_only` stays a future opt-in.
- closed-not-blessed: (3) **grid top-pack vs CTk equal-weight spread** — resolved by adding grid row/column weights in [CXC-RM-M4], so the engine can reproduce CTk's fill; the actual look is chosen live later.
- status: operational
- part-of: [PROJECT:CXC-ROADMAP]

### [CXC-RM-M3] M3 — Browser Backend (the web unlock)
- goal: Implement Layer 1 for the browser per Decision 1 ([CXC-RM-D1]); bus over MQTT-websockets (extend `web.py`'s bridge). Because Layer 2 + widgets are shared, this is a backend + event plumbing, not a rewrite.
- unlocks: **Both** widgets-on-web **and** Composer-as-a-web-app — the same investment serves both.
- deliverables: browser Layer-1 backend (per D1); DOM events → engine events; bus-over-websocket; `.compose.yaml` rendered in-browser.
- acceptance: the same `.compose.yaml` renders pixel-identically in browser vs Skia reference ([CXC-R-C1]); interaction + live bus binding work.
- depends-on: [CXC-RM-M2], [CXC-RM-D1]
- part-of: [PROJECT:CXC-ROADMAP]

### [CXC-RM-M4] M4 — Composer on the Correct Model (desktop-first)
- goal: Rebuild Composer (the WW / WC / layers / telemetry-bar redesign in specs/ux/) on the render engine — editing `.compose.yaml` pixel-stack composites and previewing *real* engine-rendered widgets. Bus-native and Intelligence-drivable throughout.
- decoupled-from-m3 (2026-07-06, David): M4 no longer waits on the browser backend. The desktop engine is widget-complete (M2), so Composer is rebuilt on it **now** — the redesigned tool in hand on the workhorse runtimes (macOS + RPi), previewing real widgets. A browser-hosted Composer follows M3.
- design-intent: build toward the interactive pre-vis `specs/ux/composer-workshop-previs.v1.html` — the approved visual target (Widget Workshop 2/3 with pixel rulers + pixel-stack canvas; tabbed Widget Configuration 1/3 = Overview / Layers / Widgets; spanning telemetry bar with bus/MQTT/UART and Bus-Monitor pop-out).
- engine-additions (land in this pass — small, and on the Composer critical path):
  - **Grid row/column weights** — closes CTk-retirement divergence #3 ([CXC-RM-CTK-RETIRE]); default stays top-pack, a config can request equal-weight spread to match CTk.
  - **Declarative `visible:` binding** — bind any widget's existing `visible` attribute to a namespace in `.compose.yaml` (the attribute + layout support already exist; wire the generic binding). Enables the Layers-tab visibility toggles and the Red-Alert image toggle.
  - **Dialog / overlay widget** — engine-rendered modal: `visible`-bound + scrim + centered panel + z-top (pixel-stack) + hit-capture. The portable, bus-native, own-every-pixel alternative to OS dialogs.
- unlocks: The dogfooding endgame — Composer previews the exact artifact the browser and CYD will run.
- deliverables: Composer as a render-engine app; the redesigned UX; live preview = real engine render; MCP/Intelligence bridge (internal bus on desktop; websocket bus later for the web host).
- acceptance: build the M31 composite in Composer, preview renders identically to the deployed target, export `.compose.yaml`, run it on desktop-Skia (macOS/RPi). (Browser/CYD deploy follow M3/M5.)
- status: operational (first pass, 2026-07-06) — `python/composeio/composer/` package: CompositeDocument (the pixel-stack composite model; nested-dialect .compose.yaml serialization, save→load→save byte-identical per [DP-CXC-7]) + ComposerCore (headless dual-bus backbone on ComposeApp: command dispatcher, intelligence responders, file ops — the CTk non-visual-module architecture re-hosted without CTk) + engine-rendered chrome (WorkshopWidget with pixel rulers/0,0-at-corner/selection handles/move+resize drag; WC = real TabWidget with Overview/Layers/Widgets panels; spanning telemetry bar; Bus-Monitor = M4 DialogWidget in-window, subprocess pop-out window when MQTT bridged). Launch: `python -m composeio.composer [file]`. **Preview == deployed by construction**: the WW preview parses the exact pixel_stack spec that export writes (single source), gate-tested at ≤tolerance-2 pixel diff.
- protocol-compatibility: the engine Composer speaks the SAME `composer/*` namespaces as the CTk Composer — `composer/command/execute` (MCP `_publish_command` shape), `composer/canvas/*`, `composer/config/*`, `composer/intelligence/*` — so intelligence_mcp drives it with ZERO server changes. Composite-mode vocabulary: module_id="composite"; row/column ≡ y/x px; rowspan/columnspan ≡ h/w px; set_property visible/z_index = Layers-tab eye/reorder; WC tab = imported state `composer/wc/active_tab`.
- evidence: 203 render tests green on macOS AND RPi5 (M4 adds 24: engine-additions goldens incl. Red-Alert visible toggle + Dialog open/closed; document round-trip; bus-driven mutation; intelligence snapshots; M31 gate). M31 built via bus commands end-to-end; exported artifact committed as `render/examples/m31_workshop.compose.yaml` and runs standalone on macOS + RPi5 — **full Composer window AND standalone artifact byte-identical macOS↔RPi5 (0 px, max delta 0)**. Live-window interaction smoke 12/12 (`tests/render/smoke_m4_composer.py`: tab click, catalog add, drag-move +60/+40, SE-handle resize, eye toggle, Dialog open/scrim-dismiss; 385fps macOS full-redraw). Intelligence over REAL MQTT (NODERED_HOST) 5/5 (`smoke_m4_intelligence_mqtt.py`: remote add_widget/set_property/tab-switch/state-snapshot from a separate bus peer). RPi5 kiosk live window 59.5fps at 1440x900.
- engine-additions-status: all three landed + golden-tested in `tests/render/test_m4_engine_additions.py` (15 tests). Grid weights: `row_weights`/`column_weights` = "equal" | dict | list on GridContainer + both parser dialects; all-zero = top-pack; legacy stretch default untouched. visible: binding: bool | namespace-string (truthy) | {namespace, when, invert, initial} on any widget. DialogWidget: modal hit-capture verified (scrim swallows, panel children reachable, scrim-tap dismiss publishes "off").
- change: "Flex containers gained a grow factor (layout.grow / spec key `grow`) with CSS `flex: N` semantics (basis 0, free-space share) — an M4 layout addition beyond the three planned."
- context_for_change:
  - prior_state: "FlexContainer children always took their measured size; there was no way to express the Composer's 2/3-1/3 WW/WC split or fill-remaining-height panels."
  - reasoning: "Grid track weights fix weighted spreading INSIDE a grid, but the Composer chrome (and any module that should fill its panel) needs proportional main-axis division in a flex; basis-0 grow is the smallest primitive that provides it and is what the pre-vis's CSS grid `2fr 1fr` reduces to."
  - rejected_alternative: "Additive grow (keep measured basis, share only leftover) — implemented first; children that measure 'fill' leave zero leftover, so proportions silently degenerate."
  - invalidating_assumption: "That percent sizing ('66%') would have sufficed; it breaks when siblings are fixed-px (rulers, bars) since percentages don't subtract them."
- change: "Two additive `.compose.yaml` keys emitted/consumed by Composer: `visible:` on any widget (the sanctioned engine-addition #2) and `design.purpose` (metadata only; the runtime parser ignores it)."
- context_for_change:
  - prior_state: "No declarative visibility; the design block had no purpose/description field."
  - reasoning: "purpose is the Overview tab's intent text and belongs in the artifact (an Intelligence reading the file should see the design intent); it is additive metadata, unknown-key-safe in every parser."
  - invalidating_assumption: "That design-block metadata stays parser-ignored. If a future schema validation pass goes strict, register both keys in [SPEC:CIO-CONFIG-SCHEMA]."
- deferred-from-m4 (first pass): zoom/pan/measure rail tools (zoom pinned 100%); drag-reorder in Layers (arrow buttons instead of grip-drag); binding editor + namespace picker UIs (Overview shows derived read-only summaries; + New creates a default json namespace); undo/redo history module (command protocol carries do/undo; no stack yet); preview-actuation mode (WW is select-tool only — preview widgets follow the DESIGN bus live but taps edit, not actuate); multiline purpose editing; catalog search; resizable splitter (fixed 2fr/1fr); UART cluster is an honest stub; design>module>widget hierarchy collapsed to the single composite module. CTk Composer untouched (reference, per [CXC-RM-CTK-RETIRE]).
- depends-on: [CXC-RM-M2]
- part-of: [PROJECT:CXC-ROADMAP]

### [CXC-RM-BINDING-EDITOR] Composer Binding Editor + Source Tab (Composer follow-on)
- goal: The next Composer pass after the binding/behavior layer lands — give the WC real editing surfaces: (1) a **visual binding editor** (DP-CXC-3) that authors [SPEC:CXC-BIND] — namespace picker / drag-connect + behavior config (blink/pulse/rotate/… with params), never raw YAML; (2) a **Source (YAML) tab**.
- source-tab (David 2026-07-06): a 4th WC tab **Source** — a live, bidirectional YAML view of the `CompositeDocument`. The document/visual stays the source of truth (DP-CXC-2); the YAML is a synced projection (DP-CXC-7). Canvas↔YAML **selection linkage** (select a widget → scroll/highlight its block; edit a block → canvas updates). Validate-on-edit, commit-only-on-valid-parse (a half-typed edit can't corrupt visual state). **Pop-out** to a full-width own window (reuse the Bus-Monitor pop-out mechanism) for editing room. Reuses the existing byte-identical `CompositeDocument` serialization — a view + re-parse + selection link, not a from-scratch editor. Bus-native: an Intelligence editing over the document bus stays in sync too.
- also-folds-in (M4-deferred Composer polish): widget-catalog **thumbnails** (cheap — headless-render each type small, cache); **undo/redo** (port `history.py`); zoom/pan; resizable splitter; catalog search.
- depends-on: [CXC-RM-M4], [SPEC:CXC-BIND]
- spec: **[SPEC:CXC-BINDEDIT]** (`specs/ux/01-composer-binding-editor.lts`, 2026-07-06) — build-ready.
- status: **operational (2026-07-07)** — C1–C8 all PASS. Landed: engine introspection tables ([CXC-BE-INTROSPECT]); the WC **Bindings** tab (picker + literal-map editor + behavior config w/ schema-driven fields + preview-bus test states); the WC **Source** tab (engine-native YAML editor, commit-on-valid-parse, selection linkage both ways, full-width DialogWidget pop-out); raw-spec fidelity fixes (visible-binding + doc-level `variables:` passthrough, preview `$var` substitution); `is_exact:` trigger; rotated-selection AABB hint; DSL-candidate capture (`~/.composeio/dsl_candidates.jsonl`). Polish LANDED: undo/redo + catalog search; DEFERRED: drag-connect, thumbnails, zoom/pan, splitter. Evidence: 19 compliance tests (`tests/render/test_bindedit.py`), suites green macOS(251)+RPi5(247+4skip), Intelligence-over-MQTT smoke 8/8 from BOTH platforms, new chrome pixel-compared macOS↔RPi5 Δ≤1px (pop-out 0px). Ops fix: Composer MQTT client_id now unique per process (same-id peers rc=7-kick each other, dropping events).
- part-of: [PROJECT:CXC-ROADMAP]

### [CXC-RM-FLOW] Composer Flow Mode & Bus Discovery (Composer follow-on)
- goal: The Widget Workshop's **Flow mode** — a node-graph lens of the bus wiring (namespace hub nodes ↔ widget attribute ports, wires = bindings) — plus **bus discovery**: a filterable Bus·Live rail of every namespace speaking on the ComposeBus, INCLUDING traffic the design never declared, so widgets stop being deaf to the outside world.
- spec: **[SPEC:CXC-FLOW]** (`specs/ux/02-composer-flow-mode.lts`); pre-vis `specs/ux/composer-flow-previs.v2.html`.
- status: **operational (2026-07-07)** — C1–C9 all PASS. Landed: `composer/flowpanel.py` (FlowPane rail+graph as ONE widget → drag-to-wire without a cross-panel drag primitive; FlowInspectorPanel = 6th WC tab; `build_graph` pure raw-spec projection = Intelligence parity by construction) + `composer/discovery.py` (BusDiscovery: wildcard observation + `_bus/discovery` engine harvest + declared>peer>~inferred legibility) + Layout|Flow toggle (`composer/ww/mode` bus state) + `NamespaceDef.external` (subscribed-external / declare-expected, additive `external: true`) + P0 filter (substring/glob/category + emergent prefix chips + N-of-M) + Bindings-tab LIVE-ON-THE-BUS picker group. **NEW BUS PRIMITIVE (escalated, RATIFIED by David 2026-07-07 — transport-abstraction + CAN hardware-mask model in [SPEC:CXC-PATSUB]): `ComposeIOBus.subscribe_pattern` — trailing-glob-only ('prefix/*'|'*'), MQTT-native (`composeio/+/prefix/#`), delivering the actual member namespace; wired through runtime/preview for widget-family subscriptions ([CXC-FL-PATTERN]).** Bus fixes found: on_message monitors were deaf to transport arrivals; unknown external namespaces auto-created as `binary` dropped any non-binary value (now json); bare-string `visible` bindings were coerced to the eye bool on the command path. Evidence: 31 compliance tests; suites 307 macOS / 303+4skip RPi5; live-broker smoke 13/13 BOTH platforms (separate ComposeApp peer; pattern binding receives a member created AFTER authoring); 11-shot walkthrough macOS↔RPi5 Δ≤3 px/shot (stroked-circle AA class), exported artifact byte-identical. Deferred: minimap/grouping/graph-focus, persistent node positions, ComposeApp late-export wiring + discovery re-announce-on-reconnect (infra).
