### [CXC-RM-M5] M5 — Embedded Tier: Config-Driven Boot + Board Family (parallel, POC→)
- goal: Generalize the embedded backend from the one CYD into a **board-profile** abstraction — SoC (ESP32 / S3 / C-series / P4), display driver (ILI9341 / round GC9A01 / ST7701 RGB panels), panel **geometry incl. shape (rect/round)**, touch controller, and pins — all behind the one `Canvas` contract. Add the config-fetch boot (fungible firmware: fetch `.compose.yaml` from bus_storage → render) and fill the classic-CYD's missing primitives (fill_arc/paths/transforms/draw_image/opacity). A new board = a new profile, not a new rasterizer.
- board-family (David 2026-07-06): the classic CYD (ESP32 + ILI9341 240×320, 7.6 KB band buffer) is a **PROXY** for a family AND the **performance FLOOR** of the whole system — what renders acceptably on it bounds what is universally deployable. Named future target: **Adafruit Qualia ESP32-S3 + round RGB LCD (~480×480)** — the S3's PSRAM holds a **full framebuffer** (no band-rendering constraint), a **capable embedded sub-tier** closer to the Linux tier than to the classic CYD (plausibly config-driven boot + fuller widget set + some transforms).
- round-displays: the display descriptor gains **shape** (round/rect + diameter/res); the engine clips to the panel shape and offers round-friendly layouts. A **dradis on a round LCD** is the flagship embedded demo. Ties to [CXC-R-BOOT].
- sub-tiers: 'embedded' is NOT monolithic — constrained (classic ESP32/CYD) vs capable (S3-class). Effort + achievable parity scale with the board. **Do the classic-CYD generalization + config-driven boot FIRST** (David 2026-07-06); a Qualia/round profile then = 'add a profile + round geometry', not a from-scratch bring-up.
- perf-floor (deliverable): characterize the classic-CYD floor — fps, per-frame budget, max widget count/complexity that renders acceptably — since it bounds universal deployability.
- deliverables: contract-complete `ESP32Canvas`; the board-profile abstraction; config-driven boot ([CXC-R-BOOT]); widgets hand-ported to C++ as needed, pixel-verified; the perf-floor characterization.
- reuse: `cyd/` (verified on hardware 2026-07-06 — Plex atlas + current widgets match Skia to AA/RGB565 noise), `cyd_dashboard_crosscheck.py`.
- acceptance: ESP32 boots → fetches config → renders → responds to touch in <5s ([CXC-R-C9]); generic firmware renders different configs ([CXC-R-C12]).
- status: classic-CYD pass = **OPERATIONAL 2026-07-07** (hardware-verified on the attached CYD, device `(a device id, not published)`). Config-driven boot real ([CXC-R-BOOT] as-built change record: config = `bus://assets/displays/<device_id>.compose.yaml` + default fallback, RATIFIED by David 2026-07-07); ONE binary rendered THREE configs (dashboard / status board / dradis) by asset swap, incl. a LIVE 60s-re-poll scene swap (C10) and boot→frame 2.2–2.9s typical (C9; worst 14s on slow WiFi assoc). Board-profile seam landed (`cyd/include/board_profile.h`: PanelGeometry incl. `shape` rect/round + DisplayDriver + TouchDriver-with-calibration; `boards/classic_cyd.cpp` is the first profile; canvas/dispatcher/main are board-agnostic — Qualia = add `boards/qualia_s3.cpp`). Contract fill: fill_arc, draw_path/fill_path, draw_image + BMP24/32/CI16 decode_image, real set_opacity; **transforms stay documented no-ops (escalated — see the [CXC-R-DRAW] M5 change record; live rotation on this tier needs its own per-band inverse-mapping pass, or the Qualia full-framebuffer tier)**. Widgets: +Button (M2 visual port, touch-toggling), +Image, +Sprite, +Placeholder (honest stand-in; still unported: lottie-live/callout/coordinate/relay/command/text_input/checkbox/power_toggle/doc_picker/bus_monitor/tab/dialog). [CXC-R-C18] DELIVERED: dradis Lottie baked offline by the ratified evaluator (`scripts/bake_lottie_sprite.py` → CI16 frames in bus_storage) plays on-device via draw_image (~3.7fps sweep, capture on file). Pixel gate: `scripts/cyd_config_crosscheck.py` (config-driven successor to the hand-coded crosscheck) — both static configs PASS vs the Skia reference (AA/RGB565 + ≤1px bold-glyph-advance classes; solid-structural-divergence gate <1% frame). DEFERRED, logged not faked: MQTT bindings/behaviors on-device, PNG decode, flex/grid layout (CYD configs are pixel_stack compositions — exactly Composer's export format), dirty-band rendering.
- perf-floor (MEASURED 2026-07-07, the deliverable): full-frame band render (20×16-scanline bands, 27MHz SPI): **empty-scene floor 56ms (17.9fps)** = clear+transfer; per-widget adders ≈ **gauge 44ms, LED (gradient+glow) 34ms, rect/label/button ~1.2ms**; reference points: 10-widget gauge dashboard 367ms (2.7fps), 18-widget status board 154ms (6.5fps), 36 cheap widgets 100ms (10fps), dradis sprite scene 170ms (5.9fps raster / 3.7fps loop). Bounds for universal deployability: bus-refresh dashboards (~1s cadence) comfortable to ~20 mixed widgets; tap→visual response = one frame (0.15–0.6s); ANIMATION needs dirty-band rendering (unbuilt) or the sprite path; heap: ~199KB free baseline, −~10KB/decoded image, sprite budget ≤~102KB (8×80×80 CI16) — beyond that HTTP TX stalls under fragmentation (capture push now fails cleanly; was an infinite-wedge bug, fixed).
- part-of: [PROJECT:CXC-ROADMAP]
- depends-on: [CXC-RM-M1]

