### [CXC-RM-MEDIA] Planned — Media Surface (video file + webcam/stream) — heaviest, own pass
- goal: One **frame-source widget** that composites a stream of externally-decoded frames via `draw_image`, with **pluggable sources** — `file://clip.mp4` (H.264/MP4), `camera://0` (attached webcam), `rtsp://…` / `mjpeg://…` (network stream). Video and webcam are two sources of the *same* widget, not two special cases.
- why-trickier (David 2026-07-06): unlike Lottie (pure Skia via skottie), media needs external **decode/capture pipelines** (FFmpeg/PyAV or GStreamer; platform camera APIs — AVFoundation on macOS, V4L2 + HW H.264 decode on RPi/Minnow) that produce frames the engine then `draw_image`s. Heavy, non-uniform deps.
- pixel-gate exception: the widget CHROME/layout is pixel-verifiable, but decoded-video/live-camera CONTENT is NOT golden-able (H.264 decode is non-deterministic across decoders/HW; a live feed is non-reproducible). The one bounded place [CXC-R-C1]'s cross-platform pixel identity applies to the frame *around* the media, not the content. (Contrast static Image: PNG decode IS deterministic and passes the gate.)
- tiers: workhorse (macOS/RPi/MinnowBoard) real; browser via `<video>`/getUserMedia → CanvasKit; **CYD: not supported** (can't decode H.264 — poster frame or omit).
- bus-bindable controls: play/pause/seek/speed (file); device-select/connect (camera) — same state-on-bus model.
- trigger-model (David 2026-07-18): the INVOCATION is state-on-bus too, not just the transport controls. A capable device (decoder + attached display) SUBSCRIBES a semantic namespace and, in response, plays a stream to its display — the decode/play behavior lives entirely in that leaf (complexity down; intent up). Crucially the trigger MAY be a pure semantic state (`briefing = "cylon_attack"` / a scene bit), NOT necessarily a media URL: the device maps the semantic to a local asset itself. So `[CXC-RM-MEDIA]` generalizes — the bus carries INTENT (a source ref OR a higher-level semantic), the capable device owns PLAYBACK; a device without a decoder ignores it or shows the placeholder (graceful degradation, no special-case). This is "state on the bus, behavior in the (capable) widget" applied to media, and "define-once/actuate-many" (one semantic bit → a video on a capable screen, a colored alert on a CYD). NO frames ever cross the bus.
- status: planned — heaviest of the new widgets; sequence after the pure-Skia items (Lottie/SVG).
- part-of: [PROJECT:CXC-ROADMAP]

### [CXC-RM-WLED] Planned — WLED Panel as a Low-Res Render Surface (own pass, sequenced LAST)
- goal: make a WLED addressable-LED matrix (e.g. a 16×16 panel) a genuine low-res ComposeUX **render surface** — the engine composites a small Canvas framebuffer and STREAMS pixels to the panel over WLED's realtime protocol (**DDP / E1.31-sACN**), treating WLED as a dumb pixel sink. "Define once, render many" reaching all the way down to an LED grid — the cheapest possible ComposeUX display, below the CYD tier.
- why (David 2026-07-10): high wow-factor AND WLED is ubiquitous among makers, so a WLED render surface + adaptor is probably the single best open-source on-ramp (nearly every maker already has WLED on the shelf). Elevated from backlog onto the schedule for this reason.
- fit: reuses the **Canvas contract** on a tiny RGB framebuffer + a new **WLED-pixel-stream backend** (a surface/board profile, sibling to the Qualia RGB666 framebuffer tier). The DRIVEN/output side (switch presets/effects/brightness from semantic namespaces) is separate and lands earlier as the WLED adaptor in **[SPEC:CXC-HAL]** ([CXC-HAL-ACTUATE]); THIS item is the pixel-streaming surface. Round-trips the reactive-tier framebuffer learnings (dirty-band, define-once render).
- sequencing: scheduled **LAST** of the render-surface passes (after the core widget/surface work) — a wow-factor capstone, explicitly NOT a critical-path dependency and NOT backlog.
- status: scheduled (David 2026-07-10) — on the dev schedule, last; spec TBD (a WLED surface spec, or a section of the embedded-tier board-family).
- part-of: [PROJECT:CXC-ROADMAP]

### [CXC-RM-EMBED-REACTIVE] Planned — Reactive Embedded Tier (two reference boards; own spec)
- goal: make an ESP32 a LIVE ComposeUX node, not a static-config renderer — an on-device bus/MQTT client + the binding/behavior engine ported to C++ (which finally CALLS the on-chip DSL interpreter [CXC-RM-DSL] Pass 2b) + dirty-band re-rendering. Reframed from "Reactive CYD": the acceptance criterion is **two reference boards**, because a second target is what proves the board-profile seam is real (the same falsification logic as 2b-first).
- slices (revised 2026-07-10 — three ESP32 variants connected: CYD Xtensa `usbserial-3120`, Qualia S3 `usbmodem31101`, bare ESP32-C3 RISC-V `usbmodem11301`; the dispatcher's call to LEAD with the C3, separating the reactive CORE from render):
  - **R1 — reactive core on the bare ESP32-C3 (headless)**: board-agnostic bus/MQTT client + namespace store + binding/behavior eval calling the on-chip DSL. Verify: Mac publish → C3 evaluates → GPIO/serial. Isolates the core (no display to conflate) AND **re-verifies the DSL on RISC-V** (2b was Xtensa-only).
  - **R2 — output-actuator HAL on the C3 → bring up the two built actuator boards** ((a local path, not published)): lego_dots (12× BC337 lights, Output Tier 1) then rack_triple_gauge (steppers via MCP23017/L293D, Output Tier 2). Grounds [CXC-HAL-ACTUATE] on real hardware.
  - **R3 — render integration on the CYD**: the proven core + bind→widget-attr + dirty-band re-render (leverages the working M5 renderer). Verify: publish → a gauge moves on the CYD screen.
  - **R4 — core on the ESP32-S3** (Qualia, headless): quick port of the proven core to the third variant — the Qualia display's foundation.
  - **R5 — Qualia RGB666 display**: the hard parallel-panel/framebuffer piece (also unlocks live transforms), on a proven core. Fallback if RGB-parallel is fiddly: a plain S3 + SPI display.
  - **deferred (David 2026-07-10): the CH32V003 relayed daughtercard** (button_matrix_4x4) — focus on the ESP32-C3 boards first; the CH32 model is captured ([CXC-HAL-TOPOLOGY]) and waits.
- why C3-first (not CYD-first): three suspects collapse to two — a bare headless C3 isolates "does the reactive core run on silicon" from "does render integration work"; and the C3 is the real target for two soldered-and-waiting actuator boards, so its bring-up delivers working hardware, not just a test.
- retires: dev-plan §8-A (reactive) + the live-transforms deferral, on the more-capable tier; the classic CYD proves the floor.
- device-model (David 2026-07-10, [CXC-HAL-DEVICE]): the reactive tier gives a device its **local bus**, which makes headed/headless and emit-scope orthogonal — the CYD (headed, with 4-pin JST peripheral connectors) can render AND read HAL sensors AND choose per-namespace whether a reading stays local (self-contained, works disconnected) or bridges to the shared ComposeBus. A device config becomes a composition (render widgets + HAL descriptors + logic + a bridge policy); this tier is where the display-config ([CXC-R-BOOT]) and headless-roster ([CXC-HW-DEPLOY]) paths would converge.
- participation spectrum (David 2026-07-10, [CXC-HAL-TOPOLOGY]): the phase spans embedded ComposeBus *participation*, not just the reactive-render port. Top: a capable MCU (CYD/Qualia ESP32) runs the full reactive engine + render. **Floor: the CH32V003** (the ~10¢ RISC-V chip that inspired ComposeIO), below the reactive-engine RAM floor — it does peripheral management (16-switch matrix via 2× MCP23017, R503 enrollment) and participates as **first-class-minimal** (compiled semantic mapping over CAN, no on-chip DSL) OR **relayed** (a HAL peripheral over I2C/serial to an ESP32/MinnowBoard host that maps it to the bus). A trivial 2×20-LCD "head" is a text-output HAL peripheral, not a Canvas surface. Fold-in target: a CH32V003 slice (first-class-CAN-emitter and/or relayed-HAL-peripheral) alongside the CYD/Qualia reactive slices — same semantic contract, chosen topology.
- grounded in 3 real boards ((a local path, not published), reviewed 2026-07-10, [CXC-HAL-ACTUATE]): **button_matrix_4x4** (CH32V003 relayed daughtercard — 16 illuminated switches via 2× MCP23017, UART to a host ESP32); **rack_triple_gauge** + **lego_dots** (first-class **ESP32-C3 SuperMini** actuator boards — 3 stepper gauges via L293D, and 12× BC337 light switches). Refinements: the HAL has a symmetric **output-actuator** side (GPIO/PWM/relay/stepper), and physical actuation is "define once, actuate many" — a stepper gauge and the on-screen GaugeWidget are the SAME `gauge/value` namespace. In the shipping designs first-class = ESP32-C3 (not CH32); a CH32 first-class board would ride the future CAN transport.
- gates: 2b already retired the hardest de-risk (float64 bit-exactness on Xtensa). Needs a `[SPEC:CXC-EMBED-REACTIVE]`; also reads on fleet-integrity §8-B (an on-device bus client sharpens the unauthenticated-config concern).
- status: planned — meaty Fable build; not yet dispatched.
- part-of: [PROJECT:CXC-ROADMAP]

### [CXC-RM-AUDIO] Captured — ComposeUX Audio (sound as an actuator; own spec)
- goal: a widget (headed OR headless) plays a **sound** in response to bus state — "state on the bus, sound in the widget." Sound is an **actuator output parallel to the display**: a define-once intent (a small Audio contract) realized by a per-platform backend — **I2S/DAC**, **DFPlayer-Mini** (MP3-from-SD, serial "play track N"), **MIDI synth** (SAM2695 / Seeed XIAO), **HDMI/ALSA** (RPi/MinnowBoard/desktop). The audio backend is a board-profile fact like the display driver.
- headless fit: a sound-only ESP32 (DFPlayer, no screen) is a headless ComposeUX node whose peripheral is audio — [CXC-HW-INTENT] taken at its word.
- spec: **[SPEC:CXC-AUDIO]** (`25-composeux-audio.lts`, 2026-07-10) — CONCEPT CAPTURE; framing settled, [CXC-AUDIO-OPEN] decisions (intent-set boundary, clip addressing, widget-vs-behavior shape, latency) need David's shaping before build-ready.
- fit: natural companion to [CXC-RM-EMBED-REACTIVE] (a reactive ESP32 that can also make noise).
- status: captured (David 2026-07-10); not build-ready.
- part-of: [PROJECT:CXC-ROADMAP]

### [CXC-RM-NFC] Captured — ComposeUX NFC (input peripheral; minor)
- goal: an NFC reader sees a tag and **publishes a semantic namespace** — presence + uid (+ optional NDEF payload), a value-map turning raw uid → meaning ([CXC-BIND-C8]). "Internal to the widget" vs "push to the bus" = namespace **scope**, not two mechanisms. Reader hardware (PN532/RC522 over I2C/SPI/UART, or USB/PC-SC) is a board-profile fact like the display/audio backend.
- framing: the **input dual of audio** ([CXC-RM-AUDIO]) — together they name an input/output peripheral-binding pattern (inputs publish, outputs actuate; all namespace-scoped, all board-profile). NFC is the first explicit input-peripheral beyond touch.
- spec: **[SPEC:CXC-NFC]** (`26-composeux-nfc.lts`, 2026-07-10) — CONCEPT CAPTURE; small. [CXC-NFC-OPEN]: payload depth, tag-writing, presence/debounce, and the UID-is-an-identifier-not-an-authenticator security note.
- fit: natural with the MinnowBoard lure sensors + the embedded-reactive tier.
- status: captured (David 2026-07-10); minor, not build-ready.
- part-of: [PROJECT:CXC-ROADMAP]

### [CXC-RM-HAL] Captured — Peripheral HAL (tiered sensor abstraction; own spec)
- goal: make binding a physical sensor to a namespace CHEAP — a tiered HAL so the long tail of value/edge sensors is config-only. **Tier 1 declarative** (GPIO/ADC value/edge: reed, PIR, hall, pot, thermistor — a descriptor reads/debounces/scales/maps→publishes, zero pipeline code); **Tier 2 HAL + reusable chip driver** (I2C/SPI register parts: BME280, VL53L0X, and NFC/PN532 [CXC-RM-NFC] lives here); **Tier 3 direct integration** (stateful protocol devices: R503 fingerprint, GPS — a driver exposing bus commands+events). Boundary test: value/event = HAL, operations/state/protocol = direct. The seam is **per-interaction-face** — R503's scan face is HAL-shaped, its enroll/manage face is Tier 3.
- framing: generalizes [CXC-NFC-PATTERN]; the input dual of the display/audio actuator backends. Define-once descriptor over per-platform drivers (C++ on MCU, Python/libgpiod on MinnowBoard/Pi — the lure I2C/serial is the transport). Board-profile fact like the display driver.
- spec: **[SPEC:CXC-HAL]** (`27-composeux-peripheral-hal.lts`, 2026-07-10) — CONCEPT CAPTURE; [CXC-HAL-OPEN]: descriptor schema/home, driver registry, debounce/scale knobs, direct-integration command convention, HAL-vs-headless overlap.
- fit: high-leverage companion to [CXC-RM-EMBED-REACTIVE] (it's what makes "bind reality in incrementally" easy); realizes the MinnowBoard lure-sensor role.
- status: captured (David 2026-07-10); not build-ready.
- part-of: [PROJECT:CXC-ROADMAP]

### [CXC-RM-BRINGUP] Captured — Board Bring-Up as a Descriptor-Driven Surface (own spec)
- goal: systematize board bring-up — from an ad-hoc flash loop rediscovered per device to a **descriptor-driven discipline** + a generalized ComposeUX control surface that stands up ANY node (Linux SBC or MCU) from ONE machine-readable per-board descriptor. Generalizes [minnow-bringup] from "provision a MinnowBoard" to "bring up any board."
- grounded: FOUR real boards this cycle (CYD, Qualia S3, ESP32-C3 ×3, CH32V203) — the schema is proven, not hypothetical; four divergent ad-hoc shapes reconciled into one.
- model: the per-board descriptor is the **single source** (the markdown recipe demotes to a generated view); a **two-tier verdict** gates acceptance — `verify.machine` (serial pass-tokens, wchisp verify, capture-pixel-diff) is necessary but **machine-green ≠ glass-green** (sourced from the real CYD silent-SPI-ACK freeze: `[PERF]` healthy + `capture.bmp` moving while the glass was dead), so a reasoned `verify.human` eyes-on gate is load-bearing; **flash-tool + entry dispatch** off the descriptor (`esptool` auto vs `wchisp` BOOT0-reset-manual); `requires:`-from-bus reproducibility; auto-capture to `doc://fleet_devices` + Restore (the [minnow-bringup] patterns).
- spec: **[SPEC:CXC-BRINGUP]** (`31-composeux-board-bringup.lts`, 2026-07-10) — CONCEPT CAPTURE. Local-first descriptors landed (`docs/board-bringup/*.descriptor.yaml` ×4, byte-consistent schema, David-ratified 2026-07-10); bus home `doc://board_profiles/*` (push pending). [CXC-BRINGUP-OPEN]: the char-signedness DSL fix (CH32V203 3/234 canon_equality), per-unit extended-flash verify, the generic flash mcp_action schema.
- fit: the fleet-tooling companion to [CXC-RM-EMBED-REACTIVE] + [CXC-RM-RUNTIME-DIST]; unifies the Linux-SBC and MCU fleet story under one surface + one descriptor shape.
- status: captured + spec'd (David 2026-07-10); the generalized bring-up surface is the build (implementation phase).
- part-of: [PROJECT:CXC-ROADMAP]

### [CXC-RM-HEADLESS] Planned — Headless Widgets (bus-native declarative logic; own spec)
- goal: Rendering-optional widgets — the declarative alternative to a Python bus workload. Decouples logic from devices (run headless anywhere; ESP32 only for *physical* bindings). Deploy surface + 3 scheduling modes (continuous / periodic / bus-triggered). NOT Node-RED (domain-logic, not integration-hub; interop via MQTT).
- spec: **[SPEC:CXC-HEADLESS]** (`20-composeux-headless-widgets.lts`, 2026-07-07).
- build-gated: on the headless runtime + the expression DSL (headless widgets *harvest* the DSL's use-cases). Authored in Flow mode (the `FlowNode.kind=logic` hook is already in place).
- pass-1 OPERATIONAL (2026-07-07): the headless runtime + scheduler + declarative-only triad LANDED. Fable delivered `--headless` RenderApp mode (canvas nulled at the old backend seam, lazy skia import — a headless host never imports skia), one `RenderApp.tick(t)` primitive fed by three clocks (continuous 10 Hz / periodic / bus-triggered via `subscribe_pattern`), single-process cooperative scheduler (`render/engine/headless.py`), and the one-contract roster loader (`LocalFileLoader` for goldens + `BusStorageLoader` for prod — triad live-deployed to bus_storage NODERED_HOST:8420 and fetched+run end-to-end). New declarative `outputs:` (publish-on-change). Compliance C1/C3/C4/C5/C6/C8/C9/C10/C11/C12 PASS; C2 partial-as-scoped (arithmetic residue → DSL); C7 deferred. Evidence: **325 tests green macOS** (307 pre-existing incl. all visual goldens + 18 new headless), deterministic `tick(t)` goldens, `smoke_headless_mqtt.py` 5/5 against the real broker (remote peer drives `pump/damaged`/`ship/charge` and reads `jumpdrive/readiness` back). Spec bumped to v0.3. **The 6 DSL use-cases were the primary harvest** — see [CXC-RM-BEHAVIORS] dsl-gate-MET.
- pass-3 OPERATIONAL (2026-07-10) — **Flow-mode headless authoring landed** ([SPEC:CXC-FLAUTH]). A headless widget is now a `kind="logic"` node authored in Flow: static introspection → ports, first-class output wires, inline DSL-validated expr editor, schedule picker, and roster deploy to bus_storage on the SAME Pass-1 loader (write-side added). The **Confirmation observability tier** shipped in-scope — live port values (from discovery, zero new producer) + an opt-in runtime heartbeat (`_bus/headless/<rid>/health`). CXC-FLAUTH-C1…C11 PASS; **662 tests green** (+29); author→deploy→run proven in-suite AND via `smoke_flauth_mqtt.py` 9/9 on real bus_storage:8420 + MQTT:1883. Delivered by Fable. Spec → v0.2.
- pass-4 OPERATIONAL (2026-07-10) — **the Headless Monitor landed** ([SPEC:CXC-HMON]); the observability arc is COMPLETE (Confirmation Pass 3 + Diagnosis Pass 4). Producer: the runtime instruments its tick loop → publishes per-widget trace/state/health to `_bus/headless/<id>/*` (opt-in/throttled ring buffer, never per-tick), backed by a new **DSL `evaluate_traced`** (bit-exact parity with `evaluate` over all 234 corpus cases; branch-taken + dead-branch-not-evaluated recorded). Viewer: one Monitor surface (`composer/monitor.py`) with the annotated-tick hero + replayable timeline + state + health, hosted as a Flow pop-out (the Pass-3 "Inspect ▸" stub now publishes `composer/monitor/open`) and a standalone ops app. **Default-off byte-identical AND trace-ON observation-neutral** (traced==untraced event streams). **920 tests green** (+258); `smoke_hmon_mqtt.py` 11/11 on real broker. Notable new seam: the **inbound trace control plane** `_bus/headless/<wid>/trace/ctl` (first sanctioned runtime-control namespace). One flag for David: the Monitor is engine chrome (Canvas + DSL traces), not a `.compose.yaml` primitive surface — a fully-declarative Monitor is a future custom-panel-parser option.
- status: **Headless arc COMPLETE** — Pass 1 (runtime) + 2 (DSL) + 2b (DSL on silicon) + 3 (Flow authoring + Confirmation) + 4 (Monitor / Diagnosis) all OPERATIONAL. Downstream: the DSL JS/Web-tier interpreter ([CXC-RM-M3]); the hardware/edge-node frontier (audio [CXC-RM-AUDIO], NFC [CXC-RM-NFC], HAL [CXC-RM-HAL], reactive embedded tier [CXC-RM-EMBED-REACTIVE]).
- part-of: [PROJECT:CXC-ROADMAP]

### [CXC-RM-DSL] In build — Sandboxed Expression DSL (Headless Pass 2)
- goal: The sandboxed, restricted expression language that closes the 6 use-cases harvested in Headless Pass 1 ([CXC-RM-BEHAVIORS] dsl-gate-MET) — arithmetic, `ns()` lookups, comparisons, booleans, ternary, a closed 7-function set — usable at three `expr:` sites (output / binding-value / trigger-condition). It is the sanctioned middle ground between the declarative 90% and arbitrary code ([CXC-BIND-BOUNDARY] upheld).
- hard constraint: **bit-identical across CPython / C++·ESP32 / JS**, or define-once breaks. Enforced by an executable **conformance corpus** ({expr,inputs→expected}) that every backend interpreter must reproduce byte-for-byte — the golden-frame discipline ([CXC-R-C1]) applied to expression eval. float64 everywhere (no float32 shortcut on CYD); guarded div/mod-by-zero → 0.0 (never NaN); NO transcendentals in v1 (cross-libm divergence); round() pinned half-to-even.
- stateless: integration (`remaining -= rate·dt`) is a read-modify-write OUTPUT expr reading its own namespace under the [CXC-HW-RUNTIME] deterministic `tick(t)` — the bus is the state; the expression stays pure.
- spec: **[SPEC:CXC-DSL]** (`22-composeux-expression-dsl.lts`, 2026-07-07) — build-ready.
- slice: Pass 2 = Python reference interpreter + conformance corpus (the contract) + 3-site integration + triad re-author (closes [CXC-HW] C2). **Pass 2b = C++/CYD interpreter**, JS interpreter = Web tier — each its own pass, gated ONLY on passing the identical corpus.
- pass-2 OPERATIONAL (2026-07-07): Python reference interpreter `render/engine/dsl.py` (own-AST tree-walking evaluator, sandboxed by construction — malicious exprs `__import__`/attribute/subscript/unknown-call fail at PARSE); the cross-backend conformance corpus `render/engine/dsl_conformance/dsl_corpus.json` (**226 cases, IEEE-754-bit-exact**, format `composeux-dsl-conformance-v1` + language-agnostic README — the byte-contract for Pass 2b/JS); `expr:` promoted refused→sanctioned at the 3 sites; the jump-drive triad re-authored to `expr:` → **[CXC-HW] C2 CLOSED** (single-expression readiness AND, real variable-rate drain, `min()` conditional pump rate). CXC-DSL-C1…C12 all PASS. Evidence: **570 tests green macOS** (325 baseline + 245 DSL incl. the 226 corpus cases CI-enforced via `tests/render/test_dsl.py`). Delivered by Fable (agent died on an API server error at the finish line; the reference + corpus + triad were complete and green — the dispatcher wrote the pytest wrapper `test_dsl.py`, verified sandbox + C2, and committed). Spec [SPEC:CXC-DSL] → v0.2.
- pass-2b OPERATIONAL (2026-07-09) — **define-once PROVEN on silicon.** C++/CYD interpreter `cyd/src/dsl.{h,cpp}` (host-compilable, `double` everywhere, own-AST recursive descent, bounded recursion for the MCU) passes the corpus byte-for-byte: **native harness 234/234** (`[env:native_dsl]` — the hardware-free CI foothold, §8-H) and **on-device 226/226 on the real ESP32 xtensa soft-double** (`(a device id, not published)`, 254 µs/case, `[env:cyd_dsl_test]`; corpus baked to a flash header via `gen_dsl_corpus_header.py`, no JSON/FS on the MCU). Expression eval now bit-identical macOS arm64 / x86_64 / ESP32. **Falsification payoff (2b-first thesis paid off):** the first independent implementation + a 30k-expr differential fuzz exposed a latent reference non-totality — `round/floor/ceil/%` of a `1e400`→inf overflow RAISED uncaught in dsl.py, outside its value|error contract. Totalized to IEEE (matches C++, consistent with guarded-div); corpus 226→234 (deterministic inf/finite only; NaN soft-float bit-parity left unpinned). Spec [SPEC:CXC-DSL] → v0.3, [CXC-DSL-SEMANTICS] change record.
- next: JS/browser interpreter arrives with the Web tier ([CXC-RM-M3]) — third corpus consumer. Pass 3 = Flow-mode authoring of the now-arithmetic-capable headless widgets ([CXC-HW-AUTHORING]).
- status: **Pass 2 + 2b OPERATIONAL** (2b 2026-07-09, on-device proven); JS (Web tier) queued, gated only on the corpus; Pass 3 (Flow authoring) follows.
- part-of: [PROJECT:CXC-ROADMAP]

